          %h3#as_rezk_completion_of_a_strict_category As Rezk completion of a strict category
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
            structure where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{hom}(m, n)
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Fin}(m) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n)
            between the standard finite sets with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            elements respectively. This strict category is not a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            %strong type of (all) finite types
            is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rezk+completion"} Rezk completion
            of the above strict category, which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+truncation"} set truncation
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            results in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            again, with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi X
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda X.\vert X \vert:\mathrm{FinType} \to \mathbb{N}
            from the definition of set truncation, so the Tarski universe type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X:\mathrm{FinType} \vdash \mathrm{El}(X)
            is defined by the standard finite type of the cardinality of the finite type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(X) \coloneqq \mathrm{Fin}(\vert X \vert)
          %p This Tarski universe is a univalent Tarski universe of finite types by definition of Rezk completion.
          %h3#as_a_homotopyterminal_type As a homotopy-terminal type
          %p
            A
            %strong univalent family of finite types
            consists of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and a type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B(x))_{x:A}
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(x)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
                function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} tr
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{tr}^B(x, y):x =_A y \to (B(x) \simeq B(y))
              %p
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
          %p
            A morphism of univalent families of finite types between univalent families of finite types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A', B')
            consists of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_A:A \to A'
            and a family of functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_B(x):B(x) \to B'(f_A(x))
          %p
            The
            %strong type of (all) finite types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{FinType}, \mathrm{El})
            is the homotopy-terminal univalent family of finite types: given any other univalent family of finite types
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_A:A \to \mathrm{FinType}
            and a unique family of functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_B(x):B(x) \to \mathrm{El}(u_A(x))
          %h3#as_a_type_universe As a type universe
          %p
            The
            %strong type of (all) finite types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{FinType}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+types"} finite types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/record+type"} record type
            where one of the fields is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            %li
              %p
                a witness
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)
                that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
          %p
            Similar to other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/record+types+with+type+fields"} record types with type fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Tarski"} a la Tarski
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Russell"} a la Russell
          %h4#a_la_tarski A la Tarski
          %p
            The type of all finite types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Tarski"} a la Tarski
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
          %p Formation rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{FinType} \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p Introduction rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{toElem}_A:\mathrm{isFinite}(A) \to \mathrm{FinType}}
          %p Elimination rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} finWitn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{El}(A) \; \mathrm{type}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{finWitn}(A):\mathrm{isFinite}(\mathrm{El}(A))}
          %p Computation rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{El}(\mathrm{toElem}_A(p)) \equiv A \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} finWitn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{finWitn}(\mathrm{toElem}_A(p)) \equiv p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}
          %p Uniqueness rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} finWitn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{toElem}_{\mathrm{El}(A)}(\mathrm{finWitn}(A)) \equiv A:\mathrm{FinType}}
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} Extensionality principle
            of the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} transport
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType} \quad \Gamma \vdash B:\mathrm{FinType}} {\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{ext}_\mathrm{FinType}(A, B):\mathrm{isEquiv}(\mathrm{transport}^\mathrm{El}(A, B))}
          %h4#a_la_russell A la Russell
          %p
            The type of all propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Russell"} a la Russell
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
          %p Formation rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{FinType} \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p Introduction rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{toElem}_A:\mathrm{isFinite}(A) \to \mathrm{FinType}}
          %p Elimination rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} finWitn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType}}{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{finWitn}(A):\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}
          %p Computation rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{toElem}_A(p) \equiv A \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} finWitn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{finWitn}(\mathrm{toElem}_A(p)) \equiv p:\mathrm{isFinite}(A)}
          %p Uniqueness rules for the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toElem
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} finWitn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{toElem}_{A}(\mathrm{finWitn}(A)) \equiv A:\mathrm{FinType}}
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} Extensionality principle
            of the type of all finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idToEquiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{FinType} \quad \Gamma \vdash B:\mathrm{FinType}} {\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{ext}_\mathrm{FinType}(A, B):\mathrm{isEquiv}(\mathrm{idToEquiv}(A, B))}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Unlike the case for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+types"} type of all types
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{FinType}
            doesn’t run into
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Girard%27s+paradox"} Girard's paradox
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{FinType}
            nor its set truncation is itself a finite type, and so isn’t
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+type"} essentially
            = succeed "-small." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{FinType}
          %h3#closure_under_type_formers Closure under type formers
          %p
            The type of finite types is closed under the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+types"} product types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+types"} sum types
          %h3#relation_to_the_natural_numbers_type Relation to the natural numbers type
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+truncation"} set truncation
            of the type of finite types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \simeq [\mathrm{FinType}]_0
          %p
            This is the type theoretic analogue of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+category"} permutation category
            resulting in the set of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
          %p
            This also means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+infinity"} axiom of infinity
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            could be defined as a resizing axiom similar to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+resizing"} propositional resizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+truncations"} set truncations
            could be defined from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}_U
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+propositions"} type of propositions
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} axinf
                    %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{axinf}_U:\sum_{\mathbb{N}:U} \mathbb{N} \simeq \left[\sum_{A:U} \mathrm{isFinite}(A)\right]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} axinf
                    %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{axinf}_U:\sum_{\mathbb{N}:U} T(\mathbb{N}) \simeq \left[\sum_{A:U} \mathrm{isFinite}(T(A))\right]_0
          %p
            The arithmetic operations and order relations on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            can be defined by induction on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+truncation"} set truncation
          %p
            For all finite types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:\mathrm{FinType}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:\mathrm{FinType}
            and finite families
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C:A \to \mathrm{FinType}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ∅
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝟙
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 =_\mathbb{N} [\emptyset]_0 \quad 1 =_\mathbb{N} [\mathbb{1}]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]_0 + [B]_0 =_\mathbb{N} [A + B]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x = 1}^{[A]_0} [C]_0(x) =_\mathbb{N} \left[\sum_{x:A} C(x)\right]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]_0 \cdot [B]_0 =_\mathbb{N} [A \times B]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x = 1}^{[A]_0} [C]_0(x) =_\mathbb{N} \left[\prod_{x:A} C(x)\right]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B]_0^{[A]_0} =_\mathbb{N} [A \to B]_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} or
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} FinType
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]_0 =_\mathbb{N} [B]_0 \coloneqq [A \simeq B]_{(-1)} \; \mathrm{or} \; [A =_\mathrm{FinType} B]_{(-1)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]_0 \leq [B]_0 \coloneqq [A \hookrightarrow B]_{(-1)}
          %h2#categorical_semantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            The categorical semantics of the type of finite types is the finite object classifier, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
            which classifies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+objects"} finite objects
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+propositions"} type of propositions
